{"paper": "2024-Tier1-13-Sep-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "A boatman rows to a place 30 km distant and back in 14 hours. He finds that he can row 10 km with the stream at the same time as 4 km against the stream. Find the speed (in km/h) of the stream.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "132°", "added": false}, {"text": "112°", "added": false}, {"text": "124°", "added": false}, {"text": "102°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Find the remainder: (1713 − 21) ÷ 18", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Simplify the following. 16 ÷ 2− 7 × 15 ÷ 3 + 5 × 5 + 4 × 3 − 10", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "230", "added": false}, {"text": "250", "added": false}, {"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "260", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "If the curved surface area of a cylinder is 880 cm2 , then the product of its height and radius is:", "options": [{"text": "90 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "120 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "220 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "140 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The angle turned by minutes hand in 25 minutes in a clock is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "A class of 30 students appeared in a test. The average score of 12 students is 62, and that of the rest is 72. What is the average score of the class?", "options": [{"text": "66", "added": false}, {"text": "68", "added": false}, {"text": "67", "added": false}, {"text": "69", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "a2 b2", "added": false}, {"text": "1-a2 b2", "added": false}, {"text": "a2 b2 +2", "added": false}, {"text": "a2 b2 +1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Two pipes P and Q can fill a tank in 36 minutes and 45 minutes, respectively. If both pipes are opened together, the time taken to fill the tank is:", "options": [{"text": "81 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "20 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "40.5 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "10 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "30,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "40,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "16,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "20,00,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question. The table displays the number of cars produced (in lakhs) by six different brands between 2018 and 2023. Brand 2018 2019 2020 2021 2022 2023 A 36 40 42 45 47 42 B 23 37 28 32 34 26 C 45 47 51 54 56 48 D 35 37 42 32 36 28 E 57 56 52 38 48 42 F 43 45 56 41 52 40 Which brand production is the highest, and in which year?", "options": [{"text": "E and 2019", "added": false}, {"text": "E and 2018", "added": false}, {"text": "C and 2022", "added": false}, {"text": "F and 2020", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A manufacturer announces a trade discount of 30% on his products for his dealers. One of the dealers purchased 6 smart phones manufactured by the company at the rate of Rs.25,000 each. What is the amount of trade discount?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.50,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.55,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,05,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.45,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Find the mean proportional of 12.96 and 0.16.", "options": [{"text": "1.21", "added": false}, {"text": "1.96", "added": false}, {"text": "1.44", "added": false}, {"text": "1.69", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The perimeters of two similar triangles ΔRST and ΔABC are 26 cm and 39 cm, respectively. If AB = 24 cm, then RS is ___.", "options": [{"text": "16 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "36 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "In the following sets, which set represents the angles of a triangle?", "options": [{"text": "{30°,60°,90°}", "added": false}, {"text": "{80°,50°,90°}", "added": false}, {"text": "{30°,50°,110°}", "added": false}, {"text": "{30°,50°,90°}", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4gh", "added": false}, {"text": "−4gh", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1276", "added": false}, {"text": "1479", "added": false}, {"text": "1113", "added": false}, {"text": "1364", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "A sum of ₹10,000 is taken as a loan by Rajesh at a rate of 15% p.a. simple interest for 2 years. But Rajesh could not repay it at the agreed time and asked for an extension of two more years. So, the lender included the interest amount for the period as principal for the next two years at the same rate of interest. The total amount paid by Rajesh at the end of 4 years is:", "options": [{"text": "₹18,590", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,900", "added": false}, {"text": "₹17,650", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,630", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The area of a sector of a circle of radius 12 cm, formed by an arc of length 7 cm is:", "options": [{"text": "42 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "84 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "21 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "28 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Kalyan spends 80% of his income. His income increases by 15% and his expenditure also increases by 5%. The percentage of increase in his savings is:", "options": [{"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "55%", "added": false}, {"text": "40%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A dishonest fruit-seller sells fruits at 20% profit but he uses 950 gm weight in place of 1 kg. What is the profit per cent?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9.5", "added": false}, {"text": "6.5", "added": false}, {"text": "8.5", "added": false}, {"text": "7.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "2 biscuits and 1 chocolate cost ₹69. 2 chocolates and 3 cups of coffee cost ₹127. 3 biscuits, 4 chocolates and 2 cups of coffee cost ₹229. Find the total cost (in ₹) of 5 biscuits, 5 chocolates and 5 cups of coffee.", "options": [{"text": "304", "added": false}, {"text": "375", "added": false}, {"text": "345", "added": false}, {"text": "355", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}]}